- Before: 1 of 4 cells passed. After: 4 of 4 passed. k6 http failures are 0 in all cells; the before-side stops come from the harness's own windowed monitor rules (S1/S3), which are unchanged.
- This matches log 391 (encoder ~88%/~62% of route CPU removed). The saturation point moved above the tested rates: 100/s and 200/s now hold on one worker in this VM.
  The new saturation point was NOT searched for: no higher profile was run. That would need a profile change, which needs owner approval.
- CPU: NOT measured per run in this A/B (the harness records none, and no sidecar ran). The per-request CPU figures stay those of log 391 (in-process, sandbox).
- Not shown here: production capacity, multi-worker behaviour, durable storage, separate generator host.

